references only declared entities (063) · Done: schema · Why: LS-2 · Risk: high · ∥: yes

==================================================================================================
0. HOW TO READ THIS FILE
==================================================================================================

NOTATION   This file reuses the local declarative notation of Artifact 067, with the CHECK line
           Artifact 069 added and the REPOSITORY CONVENTION basis label Artifact 071 added. It is
           an implementation choice, not COOLBOY12 architecture, and establishes no
           repository-wide schema language (SC-073-J). No parser exists for it.

           ELEMENT <name>        a structural element of a materialized Record
           LAYER                 ENVELOPE (universal, RMS §4) or FAMILY (Registry-model-owned)
           REQUIRED              yes | no | conditional — conditional is resolved by the domain
                                 matrix of §4
           CARDINALITY           exactly-one | absent | …
           CONSTRAINT            what a conforming value must satisfy
           CHECK                 how the constraint is checked, as Artifact 069 defines it:
                                   NATIVE    decidable from the Record alone
                                   EXTERNAL  needs evidence outside the Record; the line names
                                             who supplies it, and this contract does not claim
                                             it proven
                                   STATIC    a property of this contract, checked by reading it
           BASIS                 where the element or rule comes from:
                                   SOURCE FACT            stated by a governing source
                                   REQUIRED SYNTHESIS     forced by several source facts together
                                   REPOSITORY CONVENTION  a choice of Artifact 067, 069 or 071,
                                                          reused
                                   073 CHOICE             a representation decision of this file
           REJECT                a value that does not conform, with the rule it breaks and its
                                 CHECK

           conditional and absent are the one addition to the notation, a 073 choice: the
           FIELD-DEFINITION family is the first whose family elements depend on another element's
           value (§4).

STATUS     This contract describes the structure a materialized FIELD-DEFINITION Record must
           satisfy. It is not a FIELD-DEFINITION Record, not a SCHEMA-DEFINITION Record, not a
           CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY, not the schema of any domain Record that carries a field, not a
           field inventory, and not canonical data. It is an authored source outside canon/**
           (Roadmap §0.8; CONFLICT-F). Concrete FIELD-DEFINITION Records are committed only
           through the Mutation Coordinator (row 152) after G-CANON-R (072 FD-22). Where this
           contract differs from the Master Blueprint, the Record Model System, the Roadmap, or
           Artifact 072, those sources are right and this contract is wrong.

SPEC       Artifact 072 — docs/registry/field_definition.md — is the semantic contract this file
           encodes, consumed unchanged (H: 072). This file encodes only the structural
           consequences of the obligations 072 establishes (072 §28). Artifacts 067, 069 and 071
           are precedents for notation and representation conventions only: no semantics is
           taken from the MODEL-, KIND- or SUBTYPE-DEFINITION families, and none of those rows is
           a dependency of row 073.

==================================================================================================
1. RECORD SHAPE
==================================================================================================

FIELD-DEFINITION RECORD
├── ENVELOPE  partition · kind · object_id · slug · provenance · registry_ref · sot_class
└── FAMILY    subject_field · domain_tier · domain_model · domain_kind · definition
              ├── subject_field and the domain carriers together carry the ONE field semantic
              │   over ONE domain:
              │     universal tier   subject_field + domain_tier
              │     model tier       subject_field + domain_tier + domain_model
              │     Kind tier        subject_field + domain_tier + domain_model + domain_kind
              └── definition carries its governed field meaning

Artifact 073 defines exactly these twelve elements: the universal seven-field envelope (RMS §4)
and five family elements, two of them conditional (§4). It defines no other element.

That is the scope boundary of this contract, not a closure over everything a FIELD-DEFINITION
Record may later carry. Rows 108–110 keep their authority to establish Registry-owned evolution,
versioning, supersession and deprecation representation (§6 VERSIONABILITY; 072 VS-072-2). The
envelope, by contrast, stays exactly seven fields: no downstream Registry representation becomes
an eighth universal field (RMS §4; P-05).

One semantic context, up to four carriers. 072 requires that a FIELD-DEFINITION govern the
meaning of exactly one field over one domain, at one of RMS §14's three tiers (072 FD-1, FD-3,
FD-4), and fixes no count of structural carriers (072 RF-072-1). This contract carries that one
context in subject_field, which names the field, and in the domain carriers, which state the tier
and, where the tier requires it, the declared model and Kind. No element alone is the context.
subject_field alone is not a field identity: 072 §7 — "A field name alone does not establish one
shared semantic across models."

Three roles, never merged. The envelope element kind names this Record's own Kind — always
FIELD-DEFINITION. domain_kind names the declared Kind a Kind-tier field belongs to — for example
CHARACTER. subject_field names the field — for example status. They are different elements in
different roles. domain_tier names a field tier of RMS §14; it is not World's field tier.

Not the Record that carries the field. A World Record carries status; this contract is the
structure of the Registry Record that governs what status means, not of any Record that carries
it. Defining a field places it in no schema and no Record (072 FD-8), and this contract defines no
domain field, schema occurrence or field value for any model (P-04).

==================================================================================================
2. ENVELOPE — the universal seven (RMS §4; Artifact 033)
==================================================================================================

Types, defaults, nullability and serialization of the envelope fields are not established by the
governing sources (Artifact 033) and are not stated here.

ELEMENT     partition
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  R — the Registry partition
CHECK       NATIVE
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — a FIELD-DEFINITION is a Registry Record (RMS §10, §10.1; 072 §5, §22,
            RS-072-1)
REJECT      W, E, P, V or I — a Record of a domain model, such as a World Record that carries
            status, is never a FIELD-DEFINITION                   (FD-14, FD-16)    NATIVE

ELEMENT     kind
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  identifies the declared Registry Kind FIELD-DEFINITION (Kind 4 of RMS §10.1) — this
            Record's own Kind, never the Kind a field belongs to and never the field. The
            constraint is symbolic. No two-character Registry Kind code is established; none is
            minted here (SC-073-K).
CHECK       NATIVE against the symbolic Kind; against a code only once the Registry's codes are
            bound by their own rows (row 117; Artifact 060 writes the code schematically as <kind>)
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §10.1; Artifact 064 §11; 072 §5, §22
REJECT      SCHEMA-DEFINITION — a schema is another Registry Kind  (FD-9)            NATIVE
            CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY — a governed value set is another Registry Kind
                                                                  (FD-10)           NATIVE
            CONSTRAINT-DEFINITION or VALIDATION-RULE — a condition or a check is another
            Registry Kind                                         (FD-12, FD-13)    NATIVE
            any other Registry Kind                                                 NATIVE
            a domain Kind (for example CHARACTER) or the field (for example status) placed here
                                                                  (072 §22)         NATIVE
            any invented code (for example FD) presented as established             NATIVE

ELEMENT     object_id
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the object identity component under the universal identity grammar. It is this
            Record's identity — not the field's name, not the field's domain, not a field
            occurrence, not a Kind code (072 RS-072-1).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value
            STATIC — this contract makes no family element a substitute for it
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4, §5; 072 RS-072-1

ELEMENT     slug
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  decoration only; never identity, never the basis of resolution
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value
            STATIC — this contract gives slug no identity or resolution role
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §5; Artifact 033; 072 RS-072-1

ELEMENT     provenance
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it: this Record's own provenance capture.
            Provenance meaning is not defined here — RMS §4: "Provenance meaning is model-owned"
            — and the provenance of a Record that carries the defined field is never carried
            here (072 §7, FD-14).
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033

ELEMENT     registry_ref
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the universal envelope field, unchanged. This contract attaches no referent,
            self-reference convention, bootstrap target or resolution meaning to it, and it
            carries neither the field nor its domain.
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033 leaves its referent unresolved; Blueprint §9.4:
            reference resolution is not Registry work

ELEMENT     sot_class
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it. No value is fixed here; Artifact 073's own
            manifest SoT and Canon are not Record-level values and are not copied into it.
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033

==================================================================================================
3. FAMILY — FIELD-DEFINITION content (Registry-model-owned; not envelope fields)
==================================================================================================

subject_field, domain_tier and definition are required and exactly-one. domain_model and
domain_kind are conditional: present exactly once or absent, as §4 decides from domain_tier. No
family element has a default value. A required element may not be left empty, and an absent
conditional element is absent — not an empty value, a null placeholder or a wildcard (073
CHOICE). Types and serialization of the family elements are not established by the governing
sources and are not stated here; this contract fixes structure, not an encoding.

ELEMENT     subject_field
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  names the one field whose meaning this Record governs — for example status within
            (model, W), or registry_ref at the universal tier. The name is read only within the
            domain the domain carriers state: subject_field and the domain together are the
            semantic context (§1). The value names the field itself — never a Record or Record
            identifier (072 RF-072-5), never a Registry Record identifier, never a Kind or kind
            code, never a runtime object (RF-072-6), never a value, value set or vocabulary
            (FD-10), never a schema, a constraint or a validator (FD-9, FD-12, FD-13).
            Universal tier. When domain_tier is universal, the value is one of the seven envelope
            fields and no other:
              partition · kind · object_id · slug · provenance · registry_ref · sot_class
            RMS §14: "Three tiers: universal (the bootstrap set, seven fields) · model · Kind."
            The envelope is "the bootstrap set and no more" (RMS §4). This restricts the value
            at that tier only; it authors, schedules or enumerates no FIELD-DEFINITION Record
            (SC-073-G), and at the model and Kind tiers no closed set is defined.
            Scoped, not global. The same name in two domains is two contexts, carried by two
            Records. That the contexts differ does not establish that the two fields are
            distinct, and the shared spelling does not establish that they are one: a semantic
            is shared only where the governing sources establish it in each model that carries it
            (072 §7, FD-5; I-103). This contract requires no uniqueness of a name across domains
            and creates no global field namespace, field taxonomy or identifier grammar.
            Name form. The name is written as the governing sources or the domain's field
            architecture name the field. This contract fixes no case rule, punctuation, spelling,
            URI or handle for it (SC-073-M).
            Not a reference. subject_field names this Record's own subject. It refers to no
            declaration and no Record: Artifact 063 has no declared-field category, and a field
            is reached through its FIELD-DEFINITION (072 RF-072-2).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value; the value is not shaped as a Record identifier
            under the universal grammar (RMS §5); when domain_tier is universal, membership of
            the seven envelope names.
            EXTERNAL — that the value names a field the governing sources or the domain's field
            architecture establish (072 §23: the family does not itself establish that any field
            exists), and that it is no Kind name, kind code or runtime object. Field
            architectures and Kind rosters are the owning models' (072 FD-14; Artifact 063 §9).
            This is a content check, not reference legality, and this contract does not prove
            it.
            STATIC — subject_field alone is not treated as a semantic identity across models.
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 072 FD-1, FD-5, FD-6, FD-7, RF-072-2, RF-072-5, RF-072-6, §7,
            §23; RMS §4, §14, Appendix B. The universal-tier set is a SOURCE FACT (RMS §4, §14;
            072 §8 tier table). The identifier-shape check follows 069 and 071 (REPOSITORY
            CONVENTION). Carrying the field as its own named element and the element NAME are 073
            CHOICES.
REJECT      no value                                              (FD-1)            NATIVE
            two or more fields, e.g. status and tier together     (FD-1)            NATIVE
            a Record identifier, e.g. W-CH-…-<slug> (a domain instance)
                                                                  (RF-072-5)        NATIVE
            a Registry Record identifier, R-<kind>-…, such as a CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY Record's —
            the field is this Record's own subject, not a reference to another Record
                                                                  (RF-072-2)        NATIVE
            status or tier with domain_tier universal — World-owned, not universal
                                                                  (FD-6, FD-7)      NATIVE
            any name outside the seven with domain_tier universal  (FD-6)            NATIVE
            a Kind code, e.g. CH, World's code for CHARACTER       (FD-1)            EXTERNAL
            a field no governing source or field architecture establishes
                                                                  (072 §23)         EXTERNAL
            a running service, validator or linter named as the field
                                                                  (RF-072-6)        EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     domain_tier
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  one value from the closed set   universal | model | kind
              universal  the field's meaning holds over every Record, in all six models
              model      it holds over the Records of one declared Record Model
              kind       it holds over the Records of one declared Kind of one declared model
            These are RMS §14's three tiers and no other (072 FD-4). The tokens are local to this
            contract; they are no universal enum outside it. The token kind names the Kind tier —
            not the envelope element kind and not any Kind name.
            The tier is stated, never inferred. A Record without domain_tier does not conform:
            absence of a domain is not the universal tier, so omitting a scope can never make a
            field universal (072 FD-5).
            Not World's tier. domain_tier is not the World field tier (RMS §14; 072 FD-7), not a
            lifecycle or canonicality tier, not an authority transfer, not a semantic dependency
            and not a schema's applicable Model or Kind (072 §8).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, membership of the closed set
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §14 (the three tiers); 072 FD-3, FD-4. REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 072
            FD-5, RF-072-1 (which carriers a domain needs depends on its tier). Stating the tier
            as its own element, rather than inferring it from which carriers are present, the
            element NAME and the token spelling, taken from RMS §14's words, are 073 CHOICES
            (§6 REPRESENTATION).
REJECT      no value — a field with no tier                       (FD-3, FD-4)      NATIVE
            two or more values, e.g. model and kind together      (FD-1, FD-4)      NATIVE
            a value outside the set, e.g. a cross-model tier for a meaning several models are
            said to share — no source establishes one (072 §8)    (FD-4; I-103)     NATIVE
            the World field tier's values, e.g. FOUNDATION         (FD-7)            NATIVE

ELEMENT     domain_model
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    conditional — present when domain_tier is model or kind; absent when it is universal
CARDINALITY exactly-one when present
CONSTRAINT  one value from the closed set   W | E | P | R | V | I
              W  World       E  Epistemic   P  Production
              R  Registry    V  Visual      I  Issue
            The sovereign Record Model whose Records the field's meaning holds over. It names the
            declared Record Model itself — the six constitutionally established models are the
            declared models Artifact 063 admits (§7 row 2). It is a declaration reference, not a
            MODEL-DEFINITION reference (072 RF-072-3), not a domain Record and not a runtime
            object. It scopes subject_field and asserts nothing else about the model: it confers
            no ownership, transfers no authority and is not by itself a semantic dependency (072
            RF-072-8, RF-072-9).
            R is in the set because the Registry is one of the six sovereign Record Models. That
            this contract can represent an R-scoped field definition does not mean any is
            scheduled: no concrete R field-architecture or field-definition-set row is identified
            (SC-073-I).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence or absence as §4 requires; a single value; membership of the closed
            set. Membership is the declared-status check for a model scope: the closed set is the
            set of declared Record Models (Artifact 063 §7 row 2; RMS §2), so no external proof
            is needed.
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 072 RF-072-1 (a model-tier domain names a declared Record Model;
            a Kind-tier domain a declared Kind of one declared model), RF-072-3; RMS §2, §14.
            The closed set and carrying model scope as its own element follow 069's subject_model
            and 071's owning_model (REPOSITORY CONVENTION). The element NAME is a 073 CHOICE.
REJECT      present with domain_tier universal                    (RF-072-1)        NATIVE
            absent with domain_tier model or kind                 (RF-072-1)        NATIVE
            two or more values — ambiguous scope                  (FD-1)            NATIVE
            a value outside the set, e.g. S "Simulation" claimed as a seventh model
                                                                  (RMS §2)          NATIVE
            a Record identifier or a MODEL-DEFINITION Record identifier, R-<kind>-…
                                                                  (RF-072-3, RF-072-5)
                                                                                    NATIVE

ELEMENT     domain_kind
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    conditional — present when domain_tier is kind; absent otherwise
CARDINALITY exactly-one when present
CONSTRAINT  names one Kind exactly as the Kind taxonomy of the model in domain_model declares it —
            for example CHARACTER under W. The name is read only within domain_model. The value
            names the Kind itself — never a Record of that Kind, never the Kind's KIND-DEFINITION
            Record, never a two-character kind code (SC-073-K), never a subtype and never a
            runtime object.
            Declared status. The named Kind must be a declared Kind of domain_model, with that
            status established by the owning model's own Kind architecture (072 RF-072-1;
            Artifact 063 §7 row 3, §8.3). A FIELD-DEFINITION neither declares nor admits it, and
            creates no Kind and no subtype (072 §9; Artifact 057 §6).
            Form. domain_kind is a declaration reference to the declared Kind, not an R → R
            reference to its KIND-DEFINITION Record (072 RF-072-3; Artifact 063 §8.3). Naming it
            is not by itself a semantic dependency on the Kind's semantics (072 RF-072-9;
            Artifact 062 D-9; SC-073-E).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence or absence as §4 requires; a single value; the value is not shaped
            as a Record identifier under the universal grammar (RMS §5); the pair (domain_model,
            domain_kind) is not (W, WSV).
            EXTERNAL — declared status, and that the Kind is domain_model's. The proof comes from
            the owning model's Kind architecture (Artifact 063 SC-063-H; SC-073-L). This contract
            does not define or prove that evidence. Downstream legality validation may enforce
            this requirement under its own contract; row 112 independently enforces its narrower
            domain-instance reference prohibition. An undetermined Kind is not legal (Artifact
            063 RB-6; 072 RF-072-1, RF-072-7).
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 072 RF-072-1, RF-072-3, RF-072-9, FD-15; Artifact 063 §6, §8.3,
            SC-063-G (the form of a declaration reference is fixed by the applicable family
            contract or schema). The declaration form and naming the Kind by its declared name
            follow 069's subject_kind and 071's parent_kind (REPOSITORY CONVENTION); choosing that
            form under RF-072-3 is a 073 CHOICE (§6 REPRESENTATION). The element NAME is a 073
            CHOICE.
REJECT      present with domain_tier universal or model           (RF-072-1)        NATIVE
            absent with domain_tier kind                          (RF-072-1)        NATIVE
            two or more Kinds, e.g. CHARACTER and ORGANIZATION together
                                                                  (FD-1)            NATIVE
            a Record identifier, e.g. W-CH-…-<slug> (a domain instance)
                                                                  (RF-072-5)        NATIVE
            a KIND-DEFINITION Record's identifier, R-<kind>-…     (RF-072-3)        NATIVE
            WSV under W — the WSV singleton is not a Kind (Roadmap PART III)        NATIVE
            a name domain_model has not declared — a candidate, a rejected candidate, or a
            subtype such as GENERATED-IMAGE under V              (RF-072-1)        EXTERNAL
            a declared name under the wrong model, e.g. CHARACTER under P
                                                                  (RF-072-1)        EXTERNAL
            a running process, service or session named as the Kind
                                                                  (RF-072-6)        EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     definition
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the governed meaning of the field: what the field says about the Record that carries
            it, stated once for every Record carrying it within the domain (072 §6, §7, FD-2;
            Artifact 062 L1). Non-empty. Its internal form is not prescribed by this contract.
            It carries none of: the field's occurrence in any schema (FD-8); its type or default,
            which Blueprint §9.4 places with schema, or its cardinality, requiredness, order or
            composition, which row 078 places on the schema side (FD-9); a value, value set,
            enum or vocabulary, for any Kind (FD-10, FD-11); a condition that must hold or a
            mechanism for checking one (FD-12, FD-13); any Record, any value a Record carries or
            any current state (FD-16); the owning model's field architecture, field inventory,
            domain semantics, lifecycle, provenance meaning or canonicality (FD-14); version,
            supersession or deprecation mechanics (VS-072-2). At the universal tier it governs
            only the meaning the constitution establishes as universal and redefines no envelope
            field's presence or role (072 §7, FD-6).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, non-empty.
            EXTERNAL — the content limits are semantic and not decidable from structure; they are
            judged against 072, and this contract does not claim them proven.
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 072 §6, §7, FD-2, FD-6, FD-8 to FD-14, FD-16; RMS §6.1
            (governs; never instantiates); Blueprint §9.4 Shared field semantics row. The single
            carrier, the element NAME and the non-empty rule follow Artifacts 067, 069 and 071
            (REPOSITORY CONVENTION).
REJECT      a type, a default, or the field's cardinality, requiredness or order in a schema
                                                                  (FD-9)            EXTERNAL
            a list of allowed values, or several Kinds' value sets merged into one
                                                                  (FD-10, FD-11)    EXTERNAL
            a condition, a range, pattern or format check, or a validator procedure
                                                                  (FD-12, FD-13)    EXTERNAL
            a domain instance, domain state, derived output or runtime object as the source of
            meaning — e.g. one World Record's current status cited as what status means
                                          (FD-16, FD-17; RF-072-5, RF-072-6; 062 D-3, D-5)
                                                                                    EXTERNAL
            a statement that a field appears in, or is required by, any schema or Record
                                                                  (FD-8)            EXTERNAL
            a redefinition of an envelope field's universal role — e.g. slug made identity
                                                                  (FD-6)            EXTERNAL

==================================================================================================
4. DOMAIN MATRIX — the conditional rules
==================================================================================================

domain_tier decides which domain carriers a Record carries. The matrix is the conditional
requirement of §3 written out; every cell is checked NATIVE except where marked.

  domain_tier  domain_model        domain_kind         subject_field
  universal    absent              absent              one of the seven envelope fields
  model        exactly one,        absent              one field, read within the model
               W | E | P | R | V | I
  kind         exactly one,        exactly one;        one field, read within the Kind
               W | E | P | R | V | I                   declared by domain_model — EXTERNAL

D-01  universal: a domain_model or a domain_kind is present          → REJECT   NATIVE
D-02  model: domain_model is absent                                  → REJECT   NATIVE
D-03  model: domain_kind is present                                  → REJECT   NATIVE
D-04  kind: domain_model is absent                                   → REJECT   NATIVE
D-05  kind: domain_kind is absent                                    → REJECT   NATIVE
D-06  kind: domain_kind is not a declared Kind of domain_model       → REJECT   EXTERNAL
D-07  any tier: two values of domain_tier, domain_model or domain_kind → REJECT NATIVE
D-08  domain_tier absent or outside universal | model | kind         → REJECT   NATIVE
D-09  domain_model outside W | E | P | R | V | I                     → REJECT   NATIVE
D-10  universal: subject_field outside the seven envelope fields     → REJECT   NATIVE

BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 072 RF-072-1 (a model-tier domain names a declared Record Model;
            a Kind-tier domain names a declared Kind of one declared model; a universal-tier
            domain names neither), FD-3, FD-4, FD-6; RMS §14. The matrix form is a 073 CHOICE.

The matrix fixes scope only. It derives from the domain no type, default, range, unit, format,
enum, constraint, value-domain ontology, vocabulary relation or schema applicability (072
SC-072-G, §28; SC-073-C).

==================================================================================================
5. STRUCTURAL PROHIBITIONS
==================================================================================================

P-01A Artifact 073 introduces no element beyond the twelve of §1. A Record carrying any of the
      following does not conform (NATIVE):
      — schema-side properties (072 FD-9; Blueprint §9.4; row 078): type, datatype, default,
        required, requiredness, cardinality, order, position, nullable, occurs_in, schema_fields,
        composition;
      — value-domain content (072 FD-10, FD-11, SC-072-G): allowed_values, values, value_set,
        enum, range, unit, format, pattern;
      — conditions and checks (072 FD-12, FD-13): constraint, constraints, validation_rule,
        validation_rules, validator, regex, min, max;
      — universal semantics, ownership or runtime structure (P-03, P-06; 072 RF-072-6): status,
        tier, lifecycle_state, canonical, history, relationship_record, owner, owns_records,
        admitted, admission_rationale, field_inventory, kind_code, field_code, implementation,
        service, worker, session, process, handler.
      The element domain_tier is not tier: it states a field tier of RMS §14 (§3).
P-01B Artifact 073 introduces no version, revision, latest-version, supersession, replacement,
      deprecation, retirement, effective-date, migration, compatibility, retention or history
      element or mechanism, and no lifecycle or state machine. That representation is deferred
      to rows 108–110: neither defined nor permanently prohibited here (072 VS-072-2). Whatever
      those rows establish stays Registry-owned, is not an envelope field (P-05) and is not a
      universal semantic shared by W, E, P, V or I (P-06).
P-02  No generic reference or dependency list, and no reference the obligations of 072 do not
      require: references, refs, dependencies, related_records, definition_refs, field_refs,
      schema_ref, vocabulary_ref, controlled_vocabulary_ref, vocabulary_id, constraint_ref,
      constraint_refs, validation_ref, model_definition_ref, kind_definition_ref, kind_ref,
      model_ref. A structural reference encodes only an obligation 072 establishes — here, the
      domain scope — or representation a named downstream owner establishes; an admissible target
      category alone authorizes nothing (072 RF-072-4; Artifact 063 RB-5). This contract
      requires no vocabulary, constraint or validation reference, and forecloses none a later
      source establishes for a particular field (072 §12; SC-073-D).
P-03  No element names, carries or implies: ownership of the field, of its values or of any
      Record that carries it; a decision on which Records or schemas carry the field; admission
      of the field, the Kind or the model; or sovereignty. The owning model keeps its Records,
      their values and its field architecture; the Registry owns this Record and governs the
      field's meaning (072 FD-14). A legal reference transfers no ownership, mutation authority,
      semantic authority, admission, canonicality or source-of-truth class (072 RF-072-8).
P-04  Not the schema of any domain Record and not a SCHEMA-DEFINITION. No element carries the
      fields of any model's Records, their requiredness, cardinality, order, type or default, or
      a schema composition; those belong to the owning model's field architecture and schema
      rows and to rows 076–078 (072 FD-8, FD-9).
P-05  No envelope field added, removed or renamed. The family elements are not envelope fields,
      and no field defined by a FIELD-DEFINITION enters the envelope by being defined (RMS §4;
      072 FD-6, §22).
P-06  None of RMS §4's prohibited universal semantics: Record base, Relationship Record, History
      Record, lifecycle, canonicality, Kind taxonomy, identity composition, state model, semantic
      schema. For this family that means no universal field roster or Record base made of
      fields; no universal semantic schema assembled from field definitions; no universal
      status, tier or World mutation class; no global field taxonomy, namespace or identifier
      grammar; no forced enum across Kinds; and no Relationship Record or History Record arising
      from a field or its versions (072 §22).
P-07  Not another family's contract: not SCHEMA-DEFINITION (072 FD-9), not CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY
      (FD-10), not CONSTRAINT-DEFINITION or VALIDATION-RULE (FD-12, FD-13), and not MODEL-,
      KIND-, SUBTYPE- or RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION. No element embeds another family's
      definitions, and nothing here pre-builds rows 076–078, 081–082 or 088–091.
P-08  No element records an LS-1 or LS-2 pairing, a model field-architecture artifact or a
      lockstep partner. LS-1 is not a reference and creates no commit atomicity here, and no
      072 ↔ 073 pair exists (072 §17; SC-073-B).
P-09  No dependency element. domain_model and domain_kind are declaration references, which are
      not by themselves semantic dependencies (Artifact 062 D-9; 072 RF-072-9), and a dependency
      is not a reference field (Artifact 062 §9). Concrete dependency rules are row 111's
      (SC-073-E).
P-10  No element represents how a field comes to exist or is added, proposed, approved, admitted
      or declared. Row 459 owns the extensibility contract — "each through its own ceremony,
      never through a generic abstraction" — and Artifact 065 owns governance (072 §24 K).

