==================================================================================================
6. BOUNDARIES
==================================================================================================

REPRESENTATION  072 leaves the domain's form to 073: no element names, carrier shape, domain
                representation or discriminator are prescribed (072 §28, RF-072-3). The choices,
                each a 073 CHOICE and not a Blueprint or RMS fact:
                (1) flat carriers — subject_field, domain_tier, domain_model, domain_kind — and no
                    nested domain object, the form Artifacts 069 and 071 use for a declared-Kind
                    scope (REPOSITORY CONVENTION). A richer domain object would invite content
                    072 does not establish (SC-073-C);
                (2) an explicit tier element. Inferring the tier from which carriers are present
                    would make a Record that omits its scope a universal one; stating the tier
                    makes universal a positive, checkable claim (072 FD-5, FD-6);
                (3) the declaration form for the model and Kind scope, not an R → R reference to
                    a MODEL-DEFINITION or KIND-DEFINITION Record, and not both: a second relation
                    would be an invented one (072 RF-072-3, RF-072-4). The declaration form needs
                    no definition Record to exist first, and needs no Registry Record identifier
                    while no Registry Kind code is bound (row 117; SC-073-K).
                The form creates no semantic authority, dependency or ownership: a declared model
                or Kind named as a scope is not semantic authority for the field's meaning, and
                naming it is not by itself a semantic dependency (072 RF-072-9; Artifact 062
                D-9). The field is the Record's own subject and is carried by name, not by
                reference (072 RF-072-2).

RESOLUTION      A conforming Record carries the baseline Record identity that later
                Registry-definition resolution requires (§2): partition, kind and object_id.
                Artifact 073 does not by itself establish the complete id+version resolution
                representation: rows 108–110 retain authority over Registry evolution and version
                representation, and row 115 owns consumer resolution — "consumer resolves by
                id+version". Resolution never relies on slug, which is decoration only.
                subject_field and the domain carriers name the semantic context and do not
                thereby become this Record's identity. This contract implements no resolver,
                lookup, index, cache, storage path, fallback or version selection, and defines no
                lookup of a definition by field name or domain; row 114 owns Registry
                create/resolve/version operations — "create/resolve/version a definition".
                Resolution transfers nothing, and resolvable is not legal (Artifact 063 §11).
                (072 FD-18, RS-072-1 to RS-072-5; SC-073-M)

VERSIONABILITY  Nothing here prevents the Registry evolution and versioning model of rows 108–110
                from applying to a FIELD-DEFINITION. Artifact 073 defines no version identifier,
                numbering scheme, pinning representation, supersession, replacement or
                deprecation representation, effective date, migration, retention or
                compatibility rule, or temporal lifecycle mechanism; those decisions stay with
                rows 108 (evolution), 109 (versioning, pinning) and 110 (supersession,
                deprecation). Nor does it say whether two Records may carry the same semantic
                context — as versions of one definition, for example — or how such Records
                relate; that is theirs too. This contract is open to whatever Registry-owned
                representation those rows establish, provided it leaves the seven-field envelope
                unchanged and keeps within the Record Model boundaries (P-05, P-06); no World
                History Record is used or required (I-102). Versionable therefore means: Artifact
                073 does not structurally obstruct the evolution and versioning architecture rows
                108–110 own. Absence here is not a decision that a FIELD-DEFINITION carries no
                version. (072 FD-19, VS-072-1, VS-072-2)

REFERENCES      The one concrete reference obligation this family carries is the domain scope
                (072 RF-072-1): at the model tier, a declaration reference to a declared Record
                Model; at the Kind tier, a declaration reference to a declared Kind of that
                model; at the universal tier, none. None is an R → R reference to a definition
                Record, an owned edge or a Relationship Record (072 RF-072-3; I-102). The field
                is no reference target: there is no declared-field category (072 RF-072-2;
                Artifact 063 §7). No W/E/P/V/I domain instance, no domain state and no runtime
                instance is a target, a dependency or an authority (072 RF-072-5, RF-072-6). A
                reference transfers no ownership, admission or authority, is not by itself a
                semantic dependency, and is not legal because it resolves. An undetermined
                target is not legal. (072 FD-20, RF-072-1 to RF-072-9)

LAYER           A FIELD-DEFINITION sits at L1, shared field semantics (Artifact 062 §4.3; 072
                FD-15). No element takes meaning from L2 to L5, and this contract carries no
                dependency element (P-09). A Kind-tier or model-tier scope names a declaration;
                whether such a definition's meaning may draw on its Kind's or model's semantics
                is not established, and no dependency on L2 is asserted (072 SC-072-I; SC-073-E).

SCHEMA          This contract encodes the FIELD-DEFINITION side only: one field's meaning and
                domain. "The Registry is not schema." (Blueprint §9.4): schema is "fields, types,
                required-ness, defaults", so type and default are schema-side and are no
                FIELD-DEFINITION element. Composition, cardinality, requiredness and order are
                the schema's under row 078's Done. Row 078 owns the final SCHEMA-DEFINITION /
                FIELD-DEFINITION overlap closure exactly as its row assigns it; this contract
                does not preempt it and adds nothing to its exit criterion (072 §11, FD-9,
                SC-072-E).

VOCABULARY      No element carries a value set, a vocabulary reference or vocabulary membership.
                Per-Kind value vocabularies may diverge — "Shared structure, independent
                vocabulary" (Blueprint §9.4) — and no forced enum union is formed. Whether and how
                a field definition relates to a vocabulary is not established (072 SC-072-H;
                SC-073-D). Nothing here requires a vocabulary link, and nothing forbids one a
                later source establishes for a particular field.

VALIDATION      Field meaning is not a condition, a check or runtime enforcement (072 FD-12,
                FD-13; RMS §10.6). No constraint, validation rule, validator or check procedure is
                an element, and the NATIVE checks of this file are contract statements, not an
                implemented validator.

LS              Row 073 carries LS: LS-1 and Why: LS-2. The source-supported role is LS-2's —
                model field architecture ↔ Registry FIELD-DEFINITION (Roadmap PART III) — and this
                file is the generic structural contract concrete FIELD-DEFINITION Records conform
                to. It is not itself a lockstep partner: 072 ↔ 073 is no pair, and no LS-1
                meaning is attached to a field family (072 FD-21; SC-073-B).

MATERIALIZATION This file is an authored source. A FIELD-DEFINITION Record conforming to it is
                committed to canon/registry/** only through the Mutation Coordinator after
                G-CANON-R (Roadmap §0.8, PART X; 072 FD-22). The concrete field-definition rows
                180, 275, 302, 355 and 366 carry G: G-CANON-R. Nothing here authors or commits
                any Record, and Canon: canonical-about-meaning and CD: yes license no write
                (SC-073-F).

DOWNSTREAM      Row 073's → names all field defs: every concrete FIELD-DEFINITION Record conforms
                to this contract. Rows 180 (World field definitions, H: 179,073), 275 (E field
                definitions, H: 274,073) and 302 (P field definitions, H: 301,073) list 073 in
                their H. Rows 355 (V, H: 072,344) and 366 (I, H: 072,080,363) also author field
                definitions but do not list 073 (072 SC-072-M); their Records conform to this
                contract all the same, and their rows are not changed here. No concrete Registry
                (R) field-architecture or field-definition-set row is identified (072 SC-072-N);
                none is invented. A downstream artifact uses this contract only as its own H and
                Val allow (SC-073-H, SC-073-I).

