7. DECISION CASES (schematic — no identifier is minted; nothing here is Registry data)
==================================================================================================

ACCEPT    A  subject_field registry_ref, domain_tier universal, no domain_model, no domain_kind,
             definition carrying the field's established universal meaning. The definition does
             not redefine the envelope: the field's presence and role stay constitutional (RMS
             §4; Artifact 033), and no such Record is authored here (SC-073-G)       NATIVE
                                                     + EXTERNAL (content within FD-6)
ACCEPT    B  subject_field status, domain_tier model, domain_model W, no domain_kind — World-owned,
             not universal; its value sets may differ between World Kinds, and no vocabulary is
             encoded here                                                           NATIVE
                                                     + EXTERNAL (field established by World)
ACCEPT    C  subject_field tier, domain_tier model, domain_model W, no domain_kind — World-owned,
             not an eighth envelope field                                           NATIVE
                                                     + EXTERNAL (field established by World)
ACCEPT    D  subject_field <field>, domain_tier kind, domain_model W, domain_kind <DECLARED-KIND>
             — a placeholder: no source names a field as Kind-tier (072 §8), and none is
             asserted here                                                          NATIVE
                                         + EXTERNAL (Kind declared by World; field established)
REJECT    E  subject_field status, domain_tier universal — World status is not universal
                                                                  (FD-6, FD-7)      NATIVE
REJECT    E  subject_field tier, domain_tier universal            (FD-6, FD-7)      NATIVE
REJECT    F  domain_tier model, domain_model W, domain_kind CHARACTER — a Kind carrier is
             forbidden at the model tier                          (D-03)            NATIVE
REJECT    G  domain_tier kind, domain_kind CHARACTER, no domain_model
                                                                  (D-04)            NATIVE
BOUNDARY  H  subject_field status under (model, W) and status under (model, P) — two contexts,
             two Records. The spelling neither merges them into one semantic nor proves them two
             separately identified fields; whether a meaning is shared is the governing sources'
             to establish (072 §7, §9; I-103)                                       STATIC
BOUNDARY  I  a conforming Record with no vocabulary element — conforming: no vocabulary link is
             required, and none a later source establishes is forbidden (SC-073-D)  STATIC
BOUNDARY  J  a version element present today — not defined by this contract; its representation
             is 108–110's to establish (P-01B)                                      STATIC
BOUNDARY  K  a new field — once a model's field architecture establishes it, a Record of this
             shape can carry its meaning; how it is added is row 459's and is not represented
             here (P-10)                                                            STATIC
BOUNDARY     every NATIVE check passes but domain_kind's declared status cannot be established —
             not legal (Artifact 063 RB-6)                                          EXTERNAL
BOUNDARY     structurally conforming, not yet resolved by any consumer — the structure conforms;
             whether it resolves is row 115's, and resolvable is not legal          EXTERNAL
REJECT       domain_tier universal with domain_model W                (D-01)        NATIVE
REJECT       domain_tier kind, domain_model W, no domain_kind         (D-05)        NATIVE
REJECT       domain_tier missing; subject_field status, domain_model W (D-08)       NATIVE
REJECT       domain_model S, claimed as a seventh sovereign Record Model (D-09)     NATIVE
REJECT       subject_field W-CH-…-<slug> — a World Character Record   (RF-072-5)    NATIVE
REJECT       domain_kind R-<kind>-… — a KIND-DEFINITION Record, not the Kind (RF-072-3)
                                                                                    NATIVE
REJECT       domain_model W, domain_kind WSV — the WSV singleton is not a Kind      NATIVE
REJECT       partition W — a World Record is not a FIELD-DEFINITION                 NATIVE
REJECT       kind CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY, or kind given as an invented code such as FD
                                                                                    NATIVE
REJECT       a FAMILY element type, default or allowed_values     (P-01A)           NATIVE
REJECT       domain_model P, domain_kind CHARACTER — not declared by Production
                                                                                    EXTERNAL
REJECT       definition citing one World Record's current status as what status means
                                                                                    EXTERNAL

