8. SOURCE CONDITIONS
==================================================================================================

SC-073-A  Req: RR-27 is carried exactly; its text is unavailable (GAP-C) and is not invented
          (072 SC-072-C). Non-blocking.
SC-073-B  LS metadata. Row 073 carries LS: LS-1 and Why: LS-2; row 072 the same pattern. Roadmap
          PART III defines LS-2 as model field architecture ↔ Registry FIELD-DEFINITION and LS-1
          as every Kind spec ↔ its Registry KIND-DEFINITION (072 SC-072-D). The metadata is
          preserved exactly. No LS-1 meaning, 072 ↔ 073 pair, lockstep class, commit atomicity,
          dependency or reference is invented, and whether row 073 should carry LS-2 is not
          decided here. Recorded, not resolved; ROADMAP ISSUE, non-blocking.
SC-073-C  What a domain covers (072 SC-072-G). Only a semantic and applicability scope at one of
          RMS §14's tiers is established; the matrix of §4 encodes that and nothing more. No
          datatype, range, unit, format, enum, constraint or value-domain ontology is derived
          from it, type and default stay schema-side (Blueprint §9.4), and the relation between a
          field's domain and a schema's applicable Model and Kind is left to row 078 as input,
          not as an addition to its Done. Non-blocking.
SC-073-D  FIELD-DEFINITION and CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY (072 SC-072-H). No source fixes the
          cardinality, identity or reference relation between them. This contract carries no
          vocabulary element, requires no vocabulary link and forbids none a later source
          establishes for a particular field. Non-blocking.
SC-073-E  L1 against model and Kind scope (072 SC-072-I). Naming a model or Kind as a scope is a
          declaration reference, not a semantic dependency (Artifact 062 D-9); whether a
          model- or Kind-tier definition's meaning may draw on that Kind's semantics is not
          established. No dependency element, no dependency on L2 and no exemption from D-8 is
          asserted; concrete rules are row 111's. Non-blocking.
SC-073-F  Row 073 carries T: schema · Canon: canonical-about-meaning · CD: yes on a docs/** path.
          Artifact 003's general convention gives a docs/** specification Canon: n/a; whether it
          reaches a schema contract is not stated (072 SC-072-J). The metadata is preserved
          exactly; this file is not a Registry Record, and CD: yes licenses nothing. Recorded,
          not resolved.
SC-073-G  Universal-tier definitions (072 SC-072-L). The contract can represent a universal-tier
          FIELD-DEFINITION, and at that tier restricts subject_field to the seven envelope fields
          (RMS §14). No Roadmap row is identified that authors FIELD-DEFINITION Records for the
          seven, and Deliverable E is not in the source set. None is authored, enumerated or
          claimed scheduled here. Non-blocking.
SC-073-H  Downstream coverage (072 SC-072-M). Rows 180, 275 and 302 list 073 in their H; rows
          355 and 366 author field definitions and list 072 but not 073. → all field defs is
          preserved; the contract binds every FIELD-DEFINITION Record, whatever a row's H lists;
          no row is edited and no dependency is added. ROADMAP ISSUE, non-blocking.
SC-073-I  Registry (R) field definitions (072 SC-072-N). R is one of the six sovereign Record
          Models and may be named in domain_model; no concrete R field-architecture or R
          field-definition-set row is identified. The contract stays generic; no R artifact,
          directory, field inventory or FIELD-DEFINITION set is invented, and nothing here says
          R has or may have no fields. ROADMAP ISSUE, non-blocking.
SC-073-J  Realization and notation. The Blueprint names JSON Schema and LinkML as realization
          choices (§12.15, §26.3b). This file follows the repository's local structural-contract
          notation (§0) — Artifact 067's, with 069's CHECK line, 071's REPOSITORY CONVENTION label
          and this file's conditional and absent — and adopts no serialization, schema language
          or generated validator (072 SC-072-K). No repository-wide schema language is
          established.
SC-073-K  No two-character Registry Kind code is established, and kind codes outside World are
          not frozen (Artifact 063 §9). The envelope kind is constrained symbolically,
          domain_kind is named rather than coded, and no code is minted for a field. Identity
          binding is row 117's.
SC-073-L  Declared status has no single proof mechanism across the six models (Artifact 063
          SC-063-H). domain_kind's declared status and ownership by domain_model are therefore an
          EXTERNAL check whose proof is the owning model's. For domain_model the closed set is
          itself the declared set (Artifact 063 §7 row 2). Recorded; non-blocking.
SC-073-M  Field-name form and lookup. No source fixes the form of a field's name, and 072
          defines no lookup of a definition by field name (072 RS-072-5). subject_field carries
          the name as the sources or the domain's field architecture write it; this contract
          fixes no case rule, spelling or identifier grammar and defines no lookup. 072 RS-072-5
          names 073 beside rows 114 and 115 for how a consumer finds a field's definition; this
          contract's share is structural only — the subject and domain carriers are present on
          every conforming Record. Rows 114 and 115 own Registry operations and resolution.
          Recorded, not resolved; non-blocking.
SC-073-N  Envelope field names below the universal tier. The seven envelope fields are universal
          (RMS §4, §14), yet RMS §4 keeps "Provenance meaning is model-owned" and RMS §5 keeps
          Kind meaning model-owned. No source states whether such model-owned meaning is carried
          by a model- or Kind-tier FIELD-DEFINITION naming an envelope field. This contract
          neither requires nor forbids that structurally; any such definition must not redefine
          the envelope field's presence or universal role (072 FD-6, §7) — an EXTERNAL content
          check. Recorded, not resolved; non-blocking.

